{"ts":"2026-08-13T22:37:36.867Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2a00cb64a3a7c61d1591525b","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-swb5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The pm CLI was a runtime dependency of the web extension, so a consumer could resolve a second copy alongside the host"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"This package declared @unbrained/pm-cli in dependencies with no peer range. It is a pm extension: it ships a manifest with an entry point, calls defineExtension, and declares itself under the pm extensions key, so the host CLI loads it and the host copy is what should serve its SDK imports. Its other runtime dependencies such as express, pg and neo4j-driver are genuine and stay. As a plain dependency npm is free to install a second copy of the CLI nested under this package whenever the consumer host pin falls outside the declared range, and with no peer declaration npm had no signal that the host copy was meant to satisfy it. The same defect was reproduced concretely on the sibling pm-beads, where a host pinned to a version that package own peer floor admits ended up with two different CLI copies in one tree."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["correctness","packaging"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-13T22:37:36.867Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T22:37:36.867Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"de018f15e04316019600a4c919c4acffdd333c1dbc5